{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1521","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Nastia and a Beautiful Matrix"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You like numbers, don't you? Nastia has a lot of numbers and she wants to share them with you! Isn't it amazing?"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$a_i$$$ be how many numbers $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le k$$$) you have."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An $$$n \\times n$$$ matrix is called beautiful if it contains "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the numbers you have, and for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"each"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\times 2$$$ submatrix of the original matrix is satisfied: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The number of occupied cells doesn't exceed $$$3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The numbers on each diagonal are distinct. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Make a beautiful matrix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" size."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10\\,000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains $$$2$$$ integers $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le m, k \\le 10^5$$$) — how many numbers Nastia gave you and the length of the array $$$a$$$, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$k$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{k}$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le m$$$, $$$a_1 + a_2 + \\ldots + a_{k} = m$$$), where $$$a_i$$$ is how many numbers $$$i$$$ you have."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the sum of $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$ in one test doesn't exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each $$$t$$$ test case print a single integer $$$n$$$ — the size of the beautiful matrix."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the next $$$n$$$ lines print $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_{i, j}$$$ ($$$0 \\le b_{i, j} \\le k$$$; if position is empty, print $$$b_{i, j} = 0$$$) — the beautiful matrix $$$b$$$ you made up. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n3 4\n2 0 0 1\n15 4\n2 4 8 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4 1\n0 1\n5\n3 0 0 2 2\n3 2 3 3 0\n0 1 0 4 0\n3 0 0 0 0\n2 1 3 3 3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$0$$$ in this problem represents a blank, not a number."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples of possible answers for the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\begin{array}{cc} 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ \\end{array} \\hspace{0,5cm} \\begin{array}{cc} 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ \\end{array} \\hspace{0,5cm} \\begin{array}{cc} 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ \\end{array}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" beautiful matrices for the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\begin{array}{cc} 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 \\\\ \\end{array} \\hspace{0,5cm} \\begin{array}{cc} 4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 \\\\ \\end{array} \\hspace{0,5cm} \\begin{array}{cc} 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ \\end{array}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The example of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" beautiful matrix for the second test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\begin{array}{cc} 3 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ \\end{array}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Everything is okay, except the left-top submatrix contains $$$4$$$ numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1521E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1521/problem/E"}